<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4418" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auctĭto</span></b> , āre,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. doub.
			freq.</i> [augeo, aucto], <i>to increase</i> or <i>augment much</i> (only in the two foll. exs.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecunias faenore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					6, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			the lang. of sacrifices (cf.: augeo, auctifico, adoleo, macto,
			etc.), <i>to honor by offerings</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacris numinum potentiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, p. 220</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
